I don't know much about Power C, but if it doesn't support overlays and the
huge programming model, I would say don't waste your time.  The hack 
executable is HUGE and unless you overlay it or cut out most of the
nifty features, you will never get it to run.  If Power C is truly MS
compatible, try compiling with the MSC makefiles and see what happens, it 
might work, and it will at least give you a place to start. I have been 
fighting with the Borland compiler for a while now (it supports both 
overlays and the huge model) and I still haven't succeded in building 
an executable that will run.  If you have any more questions let me 
know.  Good luck and if you get hack to compile with Power C let me know.

